  BAI is in fact fi'o [source gisme].  The REAL question though, in
this instance, is how wide is the definition of "vanbi"?  va'o to mean
"under conditions" is perfectly acceptable when you understand that
the x1 of vanbi can be a set of circumstances or context, not simply a
physical environs.  But also remember, va'o doesn't work as a
counterfactual on its own. You must also have the da'i to mark it as
hypothetical.
         --gejyspa



